## Control {{controlId}}: Alert in the Event of an Audit Logging Process Failure

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization alerts on audit logging process failures within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant to ensure continuous audit coverage, managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if auditQueriesConfigured}}
**Automated Failure Alerting:**
Microsoft Sentinel monitoring rules detect audit logging failures:
{{#if queries}}
{{#each queries}}
- **{{name}}** — Source: {{dataSource}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Alert rules trigger notifications to {{variables.systemAdministrator}} when audit data ingestion stops, log sources become unavailable, or retention policy failures occur.
{{/if}}

{{#if sentinelNotAvailable}}
**Manual Failure Detection:**
Microsoft Sentinel is not deployed in this environment. Audit logging failure detection is performed through operational procedures:

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Daily verification that audit log sources (sign-in logs, directory audits, mailbox audits) are actively collecting data. Gaps exceeding 4 hours trigger escalation to {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Frequency:** Daily automated health check via M365 Service Health dashboard; manual verification weekly
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Audit Logging Failure Response Procedure AU-004

Alert notifications are sent via email to the Security Administrator and ISSO when audit logging failures are detected through M365 Service Health incidents or manual gap identification.
{{/if}}

**Review Frequency:** Monthly review of alert effectiveness by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine audit failure alert configurations, notification records, service health monitoring procedures, and failure response documentation.

{{#if evidenceArtifacts}}
**Evidence:**
{{#each evidenceArtifacts}}
- {{label}}
{{/each}}
{{else}}
**Evidence:** Review audit failure response records per procedure AU-004. {{evidenceArtifactUrl}}
{{/if}}
